HST Office packaging: sysui desktop integration for the "HST Office" product.

Upstream sysui/productlist.mk only knows libreoffice/libreofficedev, so no
<product>-desktop-integration.tar.gz exists for PRODUCTNAME "HST Office" and the
installer aborts with "Source for hst_office-desktop-integration.tar.gz not
found" (scp2 module_systemint.scp derives the name as lc(PRODUCTNAME), spaces
-> "_"). Changes:
 - productlist.mk/Package_share.mk: product id hst_office, UNIXFILENAME
   hst-office<MAJOR>.<MINOR>, launcher text prefix "HST", HST icon dir.
 - CustomTarget_share.mk: quote -p arguments (product name contains a space);
   pass the HST icon dir to create_tree.sh.
 - CustomTarget_deb.mk: Debian package name uses DEBNAME (no "_"); symlinks go to /usr/bin.
 - create_tree.sh: install the HST application icons, per-module PNG sizes plus
   scalable SVG (no LibreOffice icons),
   add /usr/bin/hst-office, name the mime file after the product, and skip the
   LibreOffice-named compat symlinks and appstream metainfo that would collide
   with a distribution LibreOffice.
 - menus/*.desktop: Calc -> Sheets, Impress -> Slides, start center "Office",
   plus Name[vi]; brand.pl turns %PRODUCTNAME into "HST".
 - debian/control: Maintainer HASON TECH. debian/postinst,prerm: do not rewrite
   /etc/mime.types or /etc/mailcap (upstream deletes other applications' entries).

The HST release version comes from the HST_VERSION_MAJOR/MINOR/MICRO environment
variables set by scripts/build-linux.sh (productlist.mk fails when they are unset);
PKGREVISION replaces the LibreOffice patch level in the Debian menu package version.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/sysui/productlist.mk
+++ b/sysui/productlist.mk
@@ -7,12 +7,26 @@
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 #
 
-PRODUCTLIST := libreoffice libreofficedev
-PKGVERSION := $(LIBO_VERSION_MAJOR).$(LIBO_VERSION_MINOR).$(LIBO_VERSION_MICRO)
-PKGVERSIONSHORT := $(LIBO_VERSION_MAJOR).$(LIBO_VERSION_MINOR)
-PRODUCTNAME.libreoffice := LibreOffice
-PRODUCTNAME.libreofficedev := LibreOfficeDev
-UNIXFILENAME.libreoffice := libreoffice$(PKGVERSIONSHORT)
-UNIXFILENAME.libreofficedev := libreofficedev$(PKGVERSIONSHORT)
+# HST Office: product id "hst_office" must equal lc(PRODUCTNAME with spaces -> _) because
+# the installer (scp2 module_systemint.scp) asks for <that>-desktop-integration.tar.gz.
+# The LibreOffice products are dropped so no LibreOffice-named integration is built.
+PRODUCTLIST := hst_office
+# The HST Office release version (from /VERSION) is exported by scripts/build-linux.sh;
+# it is independent of the LibreOffice engine version.
+ifeq ($(HST_VERSION_MAJOR)$(HST_VERSION_MINOR)$(HST_VERSION_MICRO),)
+$(error HST_VERSION_MAJOR/MINOR/MICRO are not set: build through scripts/build-linux.sh)
+endif
+PKGVERSION := $(HST_VERSION_MAJOR).$(HST_VERSION_MINOR).$(HST_VERSION_MICRO)
+PKGVERSIONSHORT := $(HST_VERSION_MAJOR).$(HST_VERSION_MINOR)
+PKGREVISION := 1
+PRODUCTNAME.hst_office := HST Office
+UNIXFILENAME.hst_office := hst-office$(PKGVERSIONSHORT)
+# Debian package name of the integration package (underscore is invalid there).
+DEBNAME.hst_office := hst-office
+# Text substituted for %PRODUCTNAME in launcher names: "HST Writer", "HST Sheets", ...
+DESKTOPNAME.hst_office := HST
+
+# HST brand icon set installed as the application icons (see desktop/share/create_tree.sh).
+HST_ICON_DIR ?= $(abspath $(SRCDIR)/../../assets/brand/icons)
 
